<?xml version="1.0"?>

<!--

rules must have the following format:
 <rule>
   <principal>...</principal>
   <allowedCA>...</allowedCA>
   <allowedTemplate>...</allowedTemplate>
   <allowedSanType>...</allowedSanType>
   <allowedNameSpace>...</allowedNameSpace>
 </rule>

The principal is the identity of the caller, which can be a user
or a group. Principal can be specified in the following formats:
- Distinguished Name (DN) format: CN=John Doe,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com
- User Principal Name (UPN) format: john.doe@example.com
- Security Account Manager (SAM) format: EXAMPLE\johndoe

The allowedCA is the name of the CA that the caller is allowed 
to request certificates from.

The allowedTemplate is the name of the certificate template that 
the caller is allowed to request certificates for.

The allowedSanType is the type of Subject Alternative Name (SAN) 
that the caller is allowed to request.  
The allowedNameSpace is the namespace that the caller is allowed 
to request certificates for.

allowedCA, allowedTemplate, allowedSanType, and allowedNameSpace 
can be a wildcard (*) - or empty, which means that the caller is 
allowed to request certificates from any CA, for any template, 
for any SAN type, or for any namespace, respectively.
The above elements can occur multiple times in a rule, which 
means that the caller is allowed to request certificates from any 
of the specified CAs, for any of the specified templates, for any 
of the specified SAN types, or for any of the specified namespaces, 
respectively.

The rules are evaluated in order, and the first rule that matches
the caller's identity and the requested CA, template, SAN type, 
and namespace is used to determine whether the request is allowed.

-->

<certEnrollment>
  <rules>
    <rule>
      <principal>CN=John Doe,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com</principal>
      <allowedCA>ExampleCA</allowedCA>
      <allowedTemplate>UserTemplate</allowedTemplate>
      <allowedSanType>DNS</allowedSanType>
      <allowedNameSpace>example.com</allowedNameSpace>
    </rule>
    <rule>
      <principal>CN=Jane Smith,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com</principal>
      <allowedCA>*</allowedCA>
      <allowedTemplate>*</allowedTemplate>
      <allowedSanType>*</allowedSanType>
      <allowedNameSpace>*</allowedNameSpace>
    </rule>
  </rules>
</certEnrollment>
